WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:02.716
♫ You my monkey butt fluffernutter
sweet-cheeks bunny,

00:00:02.716 --> 00:00:06.451
♫ I'm your daddy mac
snickerdoodle baby-boo honey ♫

00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:08.534
- I'm gonna say it again.

00:00:10.539 --> 00:00:12.898
When I started doing music,
it wasn’t, I didn't set out to rap.

00:00:12.898 --> 00:00:14.297
Even my producer at that time, he said,

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:17.230
"You need to spit real 'bout
your life, who you are."

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.367
And so I came out to him, I'm like,

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:21.656
“What do you—I’m gay, what if I spit about that?"

00:00:21.656 --> 00:00:23.783
He's said, “Well, then do it,
that's what you gotta do."

00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:27.533
I'm Joey Lemar AKA
Deadlee, and I'm a rapper.

00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:30.578
Oh, and I'm gay.

00:00:30.578 --> 00:00:32.661
(laughs)

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:39.518
♫ So baby, baby, I'm yours,
dirty habits, foul moods ♫

00:00:39.518 --> 00:00:42.784
Back in early 2000 when I
started doing this stuff,

00:00:42.784 --> 00:00:46.818
no one had ever seen an open gay rapper.

00:00:46.818 --> 00:00:49.006
To them, it was only supposed
to be like a masculine guy

00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:51.727
that's doing it and spitting about chicks.

00:00:51.727 --> 00:00:53.640
But I was taking it
further back with my rap,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.242
I mean I was thinking
more about Public Enemy,

00:00:56.242 --> 00:00:58.357
I was a big fan of Rage
Against the Machine,

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:01.933
I mean, they can make
change with their music,

00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:05.363
so that's kinda what I was doing, too.

00:01:05.363 --> 00:01:08.678
My early fans were not
the people who I expected.

00:01:08.678 --> 00:01:11.282
I thought it was gonna be hip-hop heads,

00:01:11.282 --> 00:01:13.750
be brown and black men,
but it wasn't that.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.824
And it kinda made me mad
because, you know, I really wanted

00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:19.997
my brown and black people
to love me and like

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:23.129
what I was doing, but I was
dealing with a lot of people

00:01:23.129 --> 00:01:26.678
that were down-low, and
they had to, 'cause that's

00:01:26.678 --> 00:01:29.540
just the way that we were
brought up, and the culture.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.039
♫ They say for better, for
worse, so baby, baby, I'm yours

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:35.021
♫ Dirty habits, foul moods,
but we keep it on course ♫

00:01:35.021 --> 00:01:37.172
When I first came out, too, I
thought I was gonna get

00:01:37.172 --> 00:01:39.274
a lot of love from the gay community,

00:01:39.274 --> 00:01:41.483
and it was the hardest thing to crack.

00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:44.425
And even the festivals, I
tried to play Long Beach,

00:01:44.425 --> 00:01:48.172
tried to play LA Pride, and
every time they're like,

00:01:48.172 --> 00:01:49.688
"You're a little too hardcore,

00:01:49.688 --> 00:01:51.682
"we don't want that element here."

00:01:51.682 --> 00:01:53.523
And I'm like, "But I'm gay, what

00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:55.145
"element are you talking about?"

00:01:55.145 --> 00:01:55.979
They don't understand that there's

00:01:55.979 --> 00:01:57.870
gay fools that look like me.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.801
And we're not gonna go
cause problems, man,

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.011
it's just this is the way we look.

00:02:02.011 --> 00:02:04.033
Did I tell you it's a love song, though?

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.030
(laughs)

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.758
It's a gay love song.

00:02:07.758 --> 00:02:08.941
Like you said, I'm sweet, man.

00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:11.244
(laughs)

00:02:11.244 --> 00:02:12.230
You know what, I think it just takes time,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.741
you need to talk to people and people need

00:02:14.741 --> 00:02:16.995
to look beyond the surface, man.

00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:18.536
And I'm guilty of that too, man, y'know,

00:02:18.536 --> 00:02:21.129
I think we're all guilty,
it's just human nature, man.

00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:23.577
I think we all wanna
put everyone in a box.

00:02:23.577 --> 00:02:26.422
And what's cool now, too, is like,

00:02:26.422 --> 00:02:29.523
dude, they're not looking
at me as the gay rapper,

00:02:29.523 --> 00:02:32.055
they're not tripping
on the whole gay thing.

00:02:32.055 --> 00:02:33.805
I'm just doing music.

